<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!--
      Overrides Tauri's generated `res/values/themes.xml` (see
      `build.rs::apply_android_overrides` — `gen/android/` is gitignored and
      regenerated by `tauri android init`, so customizations live here).

      The only change from the generated file is `windowBackground`. Stock
      `Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight.NoActionBar` sets no window background,
      so between the launcher tap and the WebView's first paint Android fills the
      window with the platform default — WHITE on a light-mode phone. That reads
      as a flash of a different app before the charcoal UI appears.

      #1e1e1e is the app's `color-bg` CSS custom property (see
      `frontend/input.css`). Keep the two in sync: the point is that the native
      window and the web page are the same color, so the handover is invisible.

      Do NOT write that token with its literal CSS double-hyphen prefix here.
      XML forbids the string "- -" (without the space) anywhere inside a
      comment, and aapt enforces it: `:app:mergeUniversalReleaseResources`
      fails the whole build on it. Nothing catches this earlier, because
      `build.rs` only COPIES this file into `gen/android/` — the copy succeeds
      and the file is only ever parsed later, by gradle.

      The night variant (`res/values-night/themes.xml`) is identical on purpose —
      the app is dark-only (`color-scheme: dark`), so it must not follow the
      system light theme here.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.omni_me_app" parent="Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#1e1e1e</item>
    </style>
</resources>
